\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Summary of all evaluation results. BGE-M3 and BERT-F1 are failure-aware means over all 142 responses per model (averaged across languages). Human /12 is the weighted mean human score across 73 evaluated rows ($\sim $24 per language; Hindi provisional). English-only failures are genuine cases (excluding English-task prompts) where the model returned English instead of the romanized target language, counted over the full $\sim $142-response set. GPT-4o is the only model with zero English-only failures across all three languages.}}{10}{table.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:summary}{{4}{10}{Summary of all evaluation results. BGE-M3 and BERT-F1 are failure-aware means over all 142 responses per model (averaged across languages). Human /12 is the weighted mean human score across 73 evaluated rows ($\sim $24 per language; Hindi provisional). English-only failures are genuine cases (excluding English-task prompts) where the model returned English instead of the romanized target language, counted over the full $\sim $142-response set. GPT-4o is the only model with zero English-only failures across all three languages}{table.4}{}}
